# Independent retained PR117 matrix replay

This prepared launcher is inactive until the current v4 collector and its
owner's frozen offline replay have both completed successfully. It never
downloads, calls authentication, executes a native artifact, or reruns a
compiler/prover/corpus. It writes only this new sibling directory, outside the
collector's six charged historical scopes. No original is copied or modified.

The accepted collector source map is
`5530745285c1b0090bf0dfb542e13b97b7279af64b78c363d1e7f11461ea7baf`
(72 identities, 16,156-byte map). Root source-review gate is
`1f46cf59a522b5b3aa1ab36fbd7b821bb9fce6f09cd204a10ad348b4b36d6fee`.
The immutable original Actions coordinate is run `37002840888`, attempt `1`,
head `10772124836b68a2df011c912b5776b2454a511f`.

Before launch, a new selection JSON names the exact current identities of
`v4/launch-completed.json`, `v4/completed/receipt.json`,
`v4/completed/final-accounting.json`, and
`pr117-completion-v4-owner-replay-1/receipt.json`. The schema is
`trident/pr117-peer-replay-selection/v1`, with those four path/bytes/SHA256
references at `inputs.{wrapper,collection,accounting,owner}`. No selection
exists while the collector is running. A separate root review must bind the
complete launcher source manifest before any execution.

`run.py --selection selection.json --review root-review.json --output <this-directory>/run-1`
uses the exact selected Python 3.14 executable to invoke the already reviewed
`v4/replay.py --collection <v4> --git-repo <R2>/final-integration/trident
--output <this-directory>/run-1/replay`.
The output must be new. The exact argv/environment is retained by the launcher.
Git reads only five blobs from the pinned original commit; replacement objects,
lazy fetching, global configuration and prompts are disabled. No credential
environment is inherited. Historical admission's isolated Python child still
uses its frozen empty-PATH environment.

The frozen checker rehashes all 37 original artifact ZIPs plus attempt logs,
their decoded member inventories and retained bytes. It replays the exact
committed native checker against 12 producer jobs and 24 generation corpus
jobs, then checks the original aggregate's 36 receipts and canonical compiler
SHA256. All earlier failed transports remain failed; 22 previously completed
archives retain their original attempt attribution, with 15 fresh artifact
readbacks and the original attempt log in v4. The native matrix's original
Rust 1.95 profile remains distinct from the final package's Rust 1.89 profile.

The new replay uses the existing 1200-second per-command bound and 8GiB free
floor. Before spawning it, all six current collector/historical scope sizes,
this peer preparation, and an additional 32MiB output reservation must fit
the unchanged 3GiB physical ceiling. No feasibility is asserted before that
actual measurement. The replay retains only its small JSON summary, five
committed source/workflow blobs, historical-admission small streams and outer
logs, with no copied ZIP/member tree. A 32MiB per-file OS limit, 32MiB sampled
aggregate output guard, 1MiB hard outer stream limits and final aggregate
checks constrain its output. The wrapper receipt itself is capped at 1MiB.
Failure is retained before owned-group cleanup; cleanup failure is separate.

The peer report exposes only source/receipt identities, native coordinates,
counts and outcome. Private HTTP headers, signed redirect URLs and raw
process diagnostics stay in their original local scopes. This is native
matrix evidence replay, with no assertion that SH8 or owner publication is
complete.
